# #156 — bidirectionality / mutation-coverage log

Each new behaviour of #156 is pinned by at least one DOM assertion. This log
records real mutation runs: a compiling mutant applied to the SOURCE, the
targeted test run, and the FAIL that proves the pin is live (not a no-op).
Every mutant was reverted via `git checkout` after capture; the trunk is clean.

Test command: `npx vitest run <file>` in the worktree.
All mutants COMPILED (tsc clean) before running — a green mutant here would mean
a coverage gap, never a broken check.

---

## M1 — strip: `countText` unsized branch invents a number

- Site: `src/ui/PackagingChainStrip.tsx` `countText` — `null ? "—"` → `null ? "0"`.
- Target: `PackagingChainStrip.dom.test.tsx` ("renders '—' … when unsized").
- Result: FAIL (killed).
  ```
   FAIL  src/ui/PackagingChainStrip.dom.test.tsx > PackagingChainStrip > renders '—' for every figure when the plan is unsized
  AssertionError: expected 'Water Extractor ×5Delivery— Water0 ×P…' to contain '— ×'
  Expected: "— ×"
  ```
  → the "never invents numbers" contract is pinned.

